Bugfix: Process valid snapshots when `copy` or `tag` encounters a missing snapshot

When a selected snapshot could not be found or loaded, `copy` and `tag`
stopped without processing the remaining snapshots. For `copy`, this also
prevented saving valid snapshots already copied into the current batch.

Both commands now process the other selected snapshots and report the
failures with a nonzero exit status afterwards. `tag` also returns an error
if modifying a snapshot's tags fails, while continuing with the remaining
snapshots. Errors while copying snapshot data still stop `copy` immediately.

https://github.com/restic/restic/issues/5071
